{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_376099eb2fa171100dac3317388f18fab5152e87e26810640d556d1922020fd6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"DuetGPT is an experimental AI-powered CLI tool and semi-autonomous agent that helps developers with coding and file system tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57b809944a359776734d03d2bbbb759fc21d290e7a2e7b28ba5bbd6c329c68e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A changelog entry indicates AI assistant responses are added to memory, and the sample interaction shows 'LLM and memory started' at launch."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b33ceec78816b1cfa5d71d9c8ce81748b124806bb367d73cd2cfb76e85e1021"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Example tasks include refactoring code, writing bash scripts, searching files for text, and drafting PR descriptions from commit messages; it is also described as a general bash helper."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7ba89c6aa92eb70aae21bb18e99cff662b735a79e569a55605d289b638b9dfae"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The approval step before command execution appears to be the product's core safety mechanism, since the README describes automatic execution only after developer approval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d1a68de2df1a07a21139e916e87ef6ebf5ff8c4101bddf20cd02a5e7cf8461a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installed globally via npm as duet-gpt and started with the duet-gpt command; on first run it prompts for an OpenAI API key."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d88f3a9f14892bc2275e3735c81cd9a84822a72a430a22d173b36d7402513227"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project no longer uses langchain, relying instead on OpenAI function calling, which the author says improved reliability and performance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df7a80fa8f76bee3f90dde48a76a7570bf3ca2b7e8736c617b2851f454236131"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Works with OpenAI models gpt-3.5-turbo-0613 (noted as not producing great code) and gpt-4-0613."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e600e51cf5eff6e022fe34badd64dbec88875b281c301479f40b88920882e042"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The 